{
"dur": 45.745,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 9.68,
"text": "In the summer of 1260, Qutuz marched north out of Egypt. On the third of September, the two armies met in a valley in Galilee, at the Spring of Goliath.",
"end": 9.955
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 9.955,
"vo_start": 10.23,
"vo_end": 15.546,
"text": "Baybars led the vanguard. He attacked, then turned and pretended to run.",
"end": 15.821
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 15.821,
"vo_start": 16.096,
"vo_end": 23.373,
"text": "It was the Mongols' own favourite trick. Kitbuqa's army chased them into the hills, where the main Mamluk army was hiding.",
"end": 23.648
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 23.648,
"vo_start": 23.923,
"vo_end": 31.123,
"text": "The Mongols almost broke through. Qutuz threw off his helmet so his men could see him, and charged, shouting 'O Islam!'",
"end": 31.398
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 31.398,
"vo_start": 31.673,
"vo_end": 35.669,
"text": "Kitbuqa was captured and killed. The Mongol army was destroyed.",
"end": 35.944
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 35.944,
"vo_start": 36.219,
"vo_end": 44.795,
"text": "It was the first time a major Mongol army had been beaten in open battle and the defeat had stuck. The Mongol advance toward Egypt stopped here.",
"end": 45.745
}
],
